  (:adr/body
  "# ADR-2607197400: PostgreSQL pool restart recovery

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

A transport failure does not make an opaque pool token invalid. The affected
lease remains usable only for release; release invalidates it, attempts the
compiled Kotoba session reset and evicts the physical channel when reset fails.
After the database becomes available, the next acquire grows a new channel and
per-connection provider instance, performing fresh TLS and SCRAM establishment.
Guest code receives no reconnect, socket or credential authority.

## Evidence

The released PostgreSQL 14.19 qualification opens and leases a pool connection,
stops the database with `pg_ctl -m fast`, observes query and release/reset fail
closed, restarts the same database, and uses the unchanged opaque pool token to
acquire a new lease and execute a query. Release and close complete with no
native transport handles remaining.

This closes graceful database restart recovery. Hard process termination,
packet loss/half-open timeout qualification, version/platform matrices and
long-duration soak remain open.")))
